{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1378360-aggravated-damage-requirements","id":1378360,"title":"Aggravated Damage requirements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-03T14:39:45-07:00","id":1378360,"title":"Aggravated Damage requirements","content":"The book says<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Aggravated Damage: Any Sphere when charged with Prime 2 and a point of Quintessence.<br /> Fire or electrical Forces Effects.<br /> Vulgar Entropy-, Life- or Prime-based Effects that directly disrupt the target\u2019s Pattern... </div> </div> </div>But in the Prime sphere says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weapons or attacks infused with Quintessence through Prime 2 Effects may hurt spirits or inflict aggravated damage, and substances infused the same way may protect against such harm. </div> </div> </div>Does this mean a Forces 2 to 3 effect that is powered by Prime 2 deal aggravated damage without needing the Quintessence point? To me inflicting aggravated damage with an effect not fire or electricity would be vulgar; am I right?<br /> <br /> For example, Benny Beatdown swings his metal bat at the eldritch abomination, and uses a Force 2/Prime 2 effect to enhance the blow (Violence as a Focus, page 413). He rolls (Attribute + Ability) to hit, and deals the damage on the Damage and Duration Chart. Is the damage Lethal (per the Forces effect) or Aggravated (because of the Prime)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3097-gator-the-unread","name":"Gator the Unread","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:07:42-07:00","id":1378402,"title":"","content":"Fire magick and damage from Entropy 4 effects are pretty much the only ways to get aggravated damage without spending quintessence. I forget about electrical if its aggravated or not. Otherwise it's always Prime 2 and a point of quintessence.<br /> <br /> Oh, just remembered, Patern ripping with Life 3 is also aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:19:57-07:00","id":1378405,"title":"","content":"As the book says, the following things deal aggravated damage:<br /> <br /> * Prime attacks in general, really - including prime-enchanted objects or weapons made out of pure prime<br /> * Any other sphere when charged with Prime 2 and a point of Quintessence<br /> <br /> Also, without Prime:<br /> * Fire or Electrical forces effects<br /> * Vulgar Entropy attacks on any pattern.<br /> * Vulgar Life attacks on a life pattern<br /> There are probably more ways, but as the book states, these are the obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-03-2020, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:14:44-07:00","id":1378430,"title":"","content":"Realize that under most circumstances listed in the sphere all the nifty Prime attacks that do aggravated damage, like weapons of pure energy and what-not, require quintessence per attack or turn.<br /> <br /> On the upside. Prine will be getting you quintessence as well so the usage for a Prime focused Mage shouldn't be a problem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:46:01-07:00","id":1378862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1378360-aggravated-damage-requirements?p=1378402#post1378402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire magick and damage from Entropy 4 effects are pretty much the only ways to get aggravated damage without spending quintessence. I forget about electrical if its aggravated or not. Otherwise it's always Prime 2 and a point of quintessence.<br /> <br /> Oh, just remembered, Patern ripping with Life 3 is also aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Toxic waste is also aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T09:39:19-07:00","id":1379008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1378360-aggravated-damage-requirements?p=1378862#post1378862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Toxic waste is also aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but, I think you need lots of Matter (like 4 or 5) to make radioactive materials, and it's not like you can <i>direct </i>radiation like a weapon without Forces anyway. You could make a pile of radioactive junk near someone assaulting you, but odds are that you're irradiating yourself, your allies, everyone in your immediate surroundings, people who walk through the area next few days. You may as well just use Forces to whomp someone(s) with fire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T13:03:01-07:00","id":1379042,"title":"","content":"I'd think that summoning up balefire/hellfire would function as aggravated damage as well. Doesn't that substitute Spirit for Prime, or does it require both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T05:36:07-07:00","id":1379238,"title":"","content":"Balefire in Cruzade was Forces 3/Spirit 3/Prime 2.<br /> <br /> It does more than just being Agg, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T11:52:52-07:00","id":1379507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1378360-aggravated-damage-requirements?p=1379008#post1379008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but, I think you need lots of Matter (like 4 or 5) to make radioactive materials, and it's not like you can <i>direct </i>radiation like a weapon without Forces anyway. You could make a pile of radioactive junk near someone assaulting you, but odds are that you're irradiating yourself, your allies, everyone in your immediate surroundings, people who walk through the area next few days. You may as well just use Forces to whomp someone(s) with fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, toxic waste isn't JUST radioactive waste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:28:09-07:00","id":1380270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1378360-aggravated-damage-requirements?p=1379507#post1379507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, toxic waste isn't JUST radioactive waste.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is a very fair and good point. I guess I never got over seeing the words &quot;toxic waste&quot; and immediately thinking of the Toxic Avenger.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}